# AI Response Style

When reviewing code:

- Be concise.
- Focus on real risks.
- Do not over-comment style-only issues.
- Do not repeat what TypeScript, ESLint, or Prettier can already catch.
- Prefer actionable suggestions.
- If uncertain, mark it as "needs human confirmation".
- For each issue, explain:
  - what is wrong
  - why it matters
  - how to fix it

Use this format:

## Risk Level
Low / Medium / High / Blocker

## Key Findings
- [Severity] File or area: issue, impact, suggestion

## Web3D-Specific Risks
- Rendering performance
- Resource lifecycle
- Interaction state
- Asset loading

## Testing Suggestions
- Suggested tests